    "payload": {
      "answer": "Leave everything intact and delete nothing. Branches and PRs are evidence and may be the only record of what the run produced -- an abandon command that removes them converts a tidy-up into data loss. Warn if a worktree directory still exists, and print its path so the operator can remove it deliberately, but never remove it automatically: vibey's worktrees are real git worktrees and deleting one out from under a live worker is a corruption, not a cleanup.",
      "item_id": "artifact_handling"
